On Wed, Jul 06, 2011 at 02:15:43PM -0700, Robin Lee Powell wrote:
> On Wed, Jul 06, 2011 at 03:42:46PM -0400, Frank wrote:
> > Am I correct in presuming the official jbofi'e fork is located at
> > https://github.com/lojban/jbofihe ?
> 
> That is a fork.  I have no idea how you mean "official", but it is
> not endorsed by the original author, who has been out of the picture
> for some time now, nor by the LLG (which is no longer in the
> business of endorsing such things), so I guess the answer is "no"?
> 
> -Robin
> 

It turns out to be as endorsed by the original author as anything
else.  After Richard ceased maintaining jbofi'e, he uploaded a few
patches and placed the code here:

  https://github.com/rc0/jbofihe

Including adding a note to top of the README describing the current
state of the software.

I have since forked that repository in:

  https://github.com/lojban/jbofihe

And that should be the place any new work happens.  I have a set of
patches I need to upload to this repository, and other than
answering the occasional question about the software, that is the
extent of my involvement with it.

If you do have patches to submit or are looking for the latest
version of jbofi'e, you found the correct one.

-Alan
